  "source": {
    "source_id": "companion:affine-gibbs",
    "anchor": "SPHMC arXiv:2609.06906v1 standingS1.E1/S2.p1.1, true RGO densityS2.Ex1, actualprox S2.E1/S4.Ex3/S4.SS1.p4.1, literalrho S4.Ex8, trueaffine law/rhocurvature S4.SS1.p4.2, scoped mode/Lip/IBP S4.SS1.p4.3 and only lastTWO4.6 inequalities S4.E6; FIRSTW2/TalagrandLSI and numericalcap/work excluded.",
    "original_text": "Exact source component with explicit truth boundary:\nFinite real Hilbert/Borel full space E, including dimension zero; any function F:E->R, any translation p:E and a real scale s!=0.\nNo continuity, measurability of F, exponential integrability, probability or moment premise. Equality is of Mathlib totalized normalized tilted measures; probability is a separate obligation for every consumer.\nThe actual pushforward of the normalized Lebesgue Gibbs tilt under x->p+s*x is the normalized Lebesgue tilt with inverse-affine potential x->F(s^-1*(x-p)). The nonzero actual Lebesgue Jacobian cancels between partition and set numerator. This canonical identity alone makes no probability assertion.\nCanonical signed affine identity for arbitrary F and nonzero scale, no eta/curvature/probability/integrability premise. The current actual SPHMC consumer separately produces allpositiveeta true posterior normalization and lastTWO4.6 moments. FIRSTW2/bias/MGF/fullLemma/main/work/composition remainOPEN; generic map identity itself is no probability assertion.",
    "text_sha256": "032094c129d3f616d7766547cd81db638c52940375a922f7541849e8c684155a"
  },
  "lean": {
    "declaration": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.AffineGibbs.map_affine_gibbs",
    "file": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Measure/AffineGibbs.lean",
    "statement": "(F : E → ℝ) (p : E) {s : ℝ} (hs : s ≠ 0) :\n    Measure.map (fun x : E => p+s • x)\n      ((volume : Measure E).tilted (fun x => -F x)) =\n      volume.tilted (fun x => -F (s⁻¹ • (x-p)))",
    "statement_sha256": "c238a3b9f8b21b49791baecedd98440dec90689fbdb590c29c9a7f159712f3db",
    "compiled": true
  },
  "blind_reconstruction": {
    "text": "Let E be a type with a normed additive commutative group structure, a real inner product space structure, finite dimension over R, and a measurable space structure equal to its Borel structure. For every arbitrary function F:E→R and every point p∈E, and for every real scalar s with s≠0, the pushforward under A(x)=p+s x of volume.tilted(x↦-F(x)) equals volume.tilted(x↦-F(s^{-1}(x-p))):\nA_*(volume.tilted(-F)) = volume.tilted(x↦-F(s^{-1}(x-p))).\nReal-vector multiplication is scalar multiplication; volume is the finite real Hilbert Lebesgue/Haar measure. For any measure nu and real function f, nu.tilted(f) literally denotes nu.withDensity(x↦ENNReal.ofReal(exp(f(x))/(∫exp(f)dnu))). This Bochner integral normalization is totalized when exponential integrability fails; the equality is equality of those literal measures. The affine map is the genuine measurable pushforward map, and the right-hand potential is composed with its inverse x↦s^{-1}(x-p). There is no CompleteSpace binder, no nontriviality assumption, and no hypothesis that F is measurable, integrable, differentiable, convex, or otherwise regular. There is no probability-measure assumption or conclusion and no assertion of exponential integrability or a positive normalization. Negative s is allowed and E may have dimension zero. The nonzero scalar is the sole explicit hypothesis after F and p; its quantifier precedes the proof argument s≠0. No Gaussian, posterior family, moment bound, or gradient conclusion occurs.",
    "text_sha256": "67b1699133273f6e7e36f0b0a7265f0420b0ca247fd47a57da4cd4d480687ac4",
    "decoder": "/root/blind_statement_decoder_28; independent source-blind mathematical statement decoder",
    "decoder_packet_sha256": "8fd6d1500dac4ed677eca55f04ee6de1a3d8be4ca6b1837321cae99863736483",
    "decoder_run_sha256": "db8561169f11d360e38c9f98942b333550fd12efe35f106dcabc12fe80925d86",
